        "original_id": "c6d83528-20e7-5eb2-bb29-0be48f972ad9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lowell George, Ian Hunter, Christopher Cross\n- Bands: Little Feat, Mott the Hoople\n- Songs and albums: Ride Like the Wind, Dixie Chicken\n\nFacts:\n- Ian Hunter Patterson, known as Ian Hunter, was born on 3 June 1939 and is a British singer-songwriter.\n- Lowell Thomas George was born on April 13, 1945 and died on June 29, 1979.\n- In 1969, Ian Hunter became the lead singer of the English rock band Mott the Hoople at its inception.\n- In 1973, Little Feat released Dixie Chicken as its third studio album.\n- Ian Hunter was the lead singer of Mott the Hoople until the band's dissolution in 1974.\n- Lowell George was an American songwriter, multi-instrumentalist, and record producer who was the primary guitarist, vocalist, and songwriter for Little Feat.\n- In 1979, Lowell George died, and Christopher Cross later dedicated Ride Like the Wind to him on the album's inner sleeve.\n- Ian Hunter returned as lead singer of Mott the Hoople for the band's reunions in 2009 and 2013.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
